2. Facts Check vs Official LIC 745
BharatSaver’s content still references Jeevan Umang “Plan 945,” which ceased Oct 2024. The current plan is “Jeevan Umang (Plan 745)”. Key official facts (LIC brochure) and gaps:

Annual Survival Benefit: 8% of Basic Sum Assured, paid yearly after PPT till maturity. (BharatSaver text: “8% of SA” – correct, but context/tag still says Plan 945.)
PPT Options: 15, 20, 25, 30 years. BharatSaver’s examples use PPT=10, which is invalid for Plan 745. Must remove or replace PPT10.
Sum Assured: Min ₹2,00,000 with multiples as per LIC. BharatSaver should mention these.
Maturity Age: 100 years (nearest birthday). BharatSaver’s content implies “till you reach age 100” (okay), but competitor text had one place “age 99” (in example). Clarify as 100.
Maturity Benefit: Lump-sum at maturity = Basic SA + vested bonuses + any Final Additional Bonus. LIC: “lump sum at time of maturity or on death”. BharatSaver says “BSA + bonuses + FAB” (fine).
Death Benefit: On death (after risk starts), nominee gets Sum Assured on death + bonuses. Policy states sum assured on death is higher of 7× annualized premium or basic SA. Also at least 105% of premiums paid. BharatSaver does not explicitly mention this. Should add the “7x rule/105%” for completeness.
Riders: Officially PWB (Premium Waiver) and AD&D riders are available; no Critical Illness rider. BharatSaver erroneously lists “Critical Illness” rider – remove it. (Competitor mentions only AD&D and PWB.)
Loan / Surrender: Official plan allows loans (up to 90% of surrender value after some years). Competitor: “Loan up to 90% after 3 years” (not in brochure snippet). BharatSaver lacks any mention. Should add that after 3 years, 90% loan against surrender value, and surrender value is defined (approx ~75% of premiums paid after 3 years).
Free Look / Grace: Standard LIC: 15-day free-look, 30-day grace. Competitor lists those; BharatSaver doesn’t. Add them for completeness.
Mismatches: In summary, BharatSaver’s page is still for Plan 945. It must be fully updated to Plan 745: change all “945” to “745,” remove PPT10 examples, delete CI rider, and add missing info (min SA, riders, loan, surrender). Official brochure confirms the 8% benefit and key terms that must be clearly restated.

